Base URL for local word:

http://127.0.0.1:8000

http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs - you can see all requests

Starting

add file .env with key

cd Backend
uvicorn main:app --reload

in Backend/index.html you can see an example (generated by ai bc I don't care)

Users

Token endpoint /auth/token

POST /users/ - register
POST /auth/token - login


json of creating a new user
{
  "firstname": "Test",
  "lastname": "User",
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "phone": "+99999999999999",
  "password": "TestPassword123!",
  "profile_picture": null,
  "dob": "2000-05-15"
}


Fields
firstname - string
lastname - string
email - string
phone - string
password - string
profile_picture string or null
dob date YYYY-MM-DD


json result
{
  "id": 1,
  "firstname": "Test",
  "lastname": "User",
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "phone": "+9999999999999",
  "profile_picture": null,
  "role": "USER",
  "dob": "2000-05-15",
  "created_at": "2026-01-01T12:00:00",
  "updated_at": "2026-01-01T12:00:00"
}


Password not returned password_hash


login

You can with email or phone
http
POST /auth/token

field

username - Email or phone
password - password

json
{
  "access_token": "<JWT_TOKEN>",
  "token_type": "bearer"
}

getting current user
http
GET /users/me

getting all user only for admin

http
GET /users/?skip=0&limit=100

getting by id, email and phone
http
GET /users/{user_id}

http
GET /users/email/{email}

http
GET /users/phone/{phone}

update user
http
PATCH /users/{user_id}


ROLE CHANGE
ONLY BY ADMIN

PATCH /users/{user_id}/role

json
{
  "role": "MENTOR"
}

We have
- USER
- MENTOR
- ADMIN

Deleting user
http
DELETE /users/{user_id}
